NAME
       holyc-eval - Evaluate one ordinary integer expression statement
       (EXPR;) at runtime IR semantics with a bounded instruction budget.

SYNOPSIS
       holyc eval [OPTION]… FILE

ARGUMENTS
       FILE (required)
           HolyC source file to read.

OPTIONS
       --command-line-source
           Make __CMD_LINE__ true at TempleOS source depths below one.

       --conditional-depth-limit=COUNT (absent=64)
           Allow at most this many nested conditional directives.

       --conditional-expression-node-limit=COUNT (absent=512)
           Allow at most this many terms and operators in one #if or #assert
           expression.

       --definition-depth-limit=COUNT (absent=64)
           Allow at most this many active definition or predefined-value
           expansions.

       --format=FORMAT (absent=human)
           Select human or JSON output.

       --generated-definition-byte-limit=BYTES, --generated-byte-limit=BYTES
       (absent=16777216)
           Allow at most this many generated replacement bytes during one
           preprocessing run. Definitions and predefined values share the
           budget.

       -I DIR, --include=DIR
           Search this directory after the compiler working directory. Repeat
           the option to add roots in order.

       --include-byte-limit=BYTES (absent=67108864)
           Reject an included source larger than this many bytes.

       --include-depth-limit=COUNT (absent=64)
           Allow at most this many simultaneously included files. The root
           file does not count toward the limit.

       --mode=MODE (absent=jit)
           Select which #ifjit or #ifaot branch the preprocessor returns.

       --predefined-date=MM/DD/YY (absent=01/01/70)
           Set the deterministic MM/DD/YY string returned by __DATE__.

       --predefined-time=HH:MM:SS (absent=00:00:00)
           Set the deterministic HH:MM:SS string returned by __TIME__.

       --step-limit=COUNT (absent=100000)
           Execute at most this many IR instructions, including terminators
           and control-flow instructions. Must be positive.

       --templeos-root=DIR
           Map TempleOS paths beginning with / or ::/ to this source-tree
           root.

COMMON OPTIONS
       --help[=FMT] (default=auto)
           Show this help in format FMT. The value FMT must be one of auto,
           pager, groff or plain. With auto, the format is pager or plain
           whenever the TERM env var is dumb or undefined.

       --version
           Show version information.

EXIT STATUS
       holyc eval exits with:

       0   on success.

       1   on an input, configuration, lowering, or evaluation error

       123 on indiscriminate errors reported on standard error.

       124 on command line parsing errors.

       125 on unexpected internal errors (bugs).

SEE ALSO
       holyc(1)

